From e5114bd8e41f70ce5b6dd98b4d0af390c9231e9b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 23:13:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(core): report a running diversion from the canonical
 noise seam (#188)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The synth diversion is canonical state (RuntimeState::diversion), but
noise_sources() — the pure definition+state seam that observations() is
built on — did not read it. The hosting seam in sim appended it instead,
so a replay or resync reconstructing a run from the snapshot and asking
the canonical seam directly got a different answer from the seat that was
running: the sim heard the diversion, the seam did not.

Read the diversion in noise_sources() and drop it from the sim's
extra_noise(), which now carries only noise canonical state does not hold
(the mole's digging and chewing). The diversion keeps its position after
the infrastructure sources, so ordering, investigation tie-breaks and
existing goldens are unchanged, and it is still gated by an unexpired
window because a restored snapshot may carry a spent record.

Also lift the sim's room_at_or_last() helper into the pure module, so the
seam and the sim resolve a noise source's room identically.

Addresses the seam half of EW-06 (option A in the issue); the scenario's
geometry and phase half was already repaired on main by #190/#203.
